> and i can't run the commandline tools: `tailscale debug ts2021`
> it show me the error log `zsh: command not found: tailscale` 

@participant10 To confirm you're encountering the same issue you can run `/Applications/Tailscale.app/Contents/MacOS/Tailscale debug ts2021` or configure an alias. See https://tailscale.com/kb/1080/cli?tab=macos#using-the-cli

@participant10 You can switch to the cli opensource version if you like, authentication and every thing with terminal works great. But it does not rely on the native VPN setup of OSX. The command has to be run in root.

Check the brew install
https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/issues/10558
